---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import RetirementModule from "../../components/RetirementModule.tsx";
import NextTool from "../../components/NextTool.astro";
import Sources from "../../components/Sources.astro";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Retirement & Roth"
  description="Everything about funding and drawing down retirement: what it will cost and whether your money lasts, when to claim Social Security, and how to choose between Roth and Traditional accounts (and grab the employer match)."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>Funding (and spending) retirement</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Retirement is two problems: building the pile, and living off it. See what your
      spending implies for the nest egg you need and whether it survives real market
      history; decide when to claim Social Security's guaranteed, inflation-adjusted
      income; and choose the account (Roth or Traditional) that keeps the most after
      tax, starting with the employer match you should never leave behind.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <RetirementModule client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The three levers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>What it costs.</strong> Flip the 4% rule around: your spending sets
          the nest egg you need (about 25× at 4%), and guaranteed income shrinks it.
          A Monte Carlo over real history shows whether the plan survives bad luck.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Social Security.</strong> Claiming later means bigger checks for
          life, inflation-adjusted longevity insurance. The breakeven age, and a
          spouse's survivor benefit, decide whether waiting pays.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Roth or Traditional.</strong> It comes down to your tax rate now vs.
          in retirement. And whatever you choose, capture the full employer match
          first: an instant, guaranteed return nothing else matches.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>Educational only, not financial advice.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Sources tool="retirement" />

  <NextTool current="/tools/retirement" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro { padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md); max-width: var(--measure); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--color-text-soft); line-height: 1.5; }
  .wl-explainer { margin-top: var(--space-lg); }
</style>
